# UI text inputs

When adding a text input (or editing one), use the shared outlined field pattern — not a bare `<input>` or a one-off style.

## Do

- Prefer `OutlinedTextField` from `src/ui/OutlinedTextField.tsx` for editable text fields (name, URL, path text, rename, etc.).
- Prefer `OutlinedSelect` / `DirectoryField` when those match the control (select / browse-for-folder).
- Keep labels, focus rings, disabled state, and validation via the shared component APIs (`error`, `trailing`, etc.).

## Don't

- Do **not** invent a new input look for dialogs or side panes.
- Do **not** use a raw `<label className="outlined-field"><span>…</span><input>` unless you are matching an existing display-only detail pattern (`<dt>`/`<dd>`), not a free-typed control.

## References

- Component: `src/ui/OutlinedTextField.tsx`
- CSS: `src/index.css` — `.outlined-field`, `.outlined-text-field`
- Examples: Settings path fields, SelectionPresetsBar rename, BackupManagerDialog snapshot name, install console Response field
